# Auto-version mobile app

When you finish a **user-facing** change under `apps/mobile/` (feature, fix, UI tweak), bump the app version before ending the task.

## How

From `apps/mobile/`:

```bash
node scripts/bump-version.js --patch
```

This updates `version.json` (semver + Android `versionCode` + iOS `buildNumber`) and syncs `package.json`. `app.config.js` reads `version.json` automatically.

## When to bump

- New menu item, screen change, bug fix, subscription/gallery/save behavior, etc.
- **Once per completed task** — not on every file edit in the same task.

## When to skip

- Docs-only, comments-only, or refactors with no release impact
- API/backend-only work (`api/`, `admin/`)
- User explicitly says not to bump

## Build vs dev

- **During development** (agent): `--patch` for visible changes
- **APK builds** (`build-apk-local.ps1`): `--build` only (already wired; use `-NoVersionBump` to skip)

Do not commit version files unless the user asks to commit.

Do not update hardcoded semver in `MD/*.md` or `README.md` — those files should reference `apps/mobile/version.json` only.
